date is expected to engage in service activities in a way that is congruent with their work as a teacher-scholar. A Ph.D. and subsequent research experience are required. The priority date for full consideration is September 14, 2026. Applicants should submit the following: 1) a cover letter addressing their motivations for teaching at a small, residential, liberal arts college; 2) curriculum vitae, including a publication list; 3) undergraduate and graduate transcripts; 4) a statement of teaching philosophy addressing approaches to classroom and laboratory courses at the introductory and intermediate level, and a new course in their specialty; 5) a statement detailing the applicant’s proposed research program (5 page maximum). In their materials, applicants should discuss how their teaching and research mentorship will foster the engagement and success of students who have varying backgrounds and interests. Applicants are encouraged to include how they will incorporate rapidly evolving technological tools (such as data analytics, cheminformatics, machine learning, or generative AI), highlighting how such tools will be leveraged to benefit teaching and learning, research, or students’ career readiness and, if relevant, any existing or potential connections with industry, government, or non-profit sectors.",
