    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194126": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics/Macro-finance/International Finance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22 Location: Granville, OH The Department of Economics at Denison University invites applications for a tenure-track position in the field of macro-finance/international finance starting August 2027. Strong candidates will demonstrate a commitment to teaching at the undergraduate level and an appreciation of the interdisciplinary nature of a small residential liberal arts institution, as well as a clear and active research agenda in the field of macro-finance and/or international finance. Primary teaching responsibilities will include core and elective courses in macro-finance, international finance and/or international trade, and courses in introductory and intermediate macroeconomic theory. The teaching load for this position is 5 courses per academic year. The Department of Economics at Denison has sixteen full-time faculty members who appreciate diverse approaches to economics. The department now offers a B.S. in Finance in addition to the B.A. and minor in Economics. For more information about the department please see: https://denison.edu/academics/economics . Denison University seeks candidates who will contribute to a vibrant academic community characterized by open inquiry, robust debate, and mutual respect. Contributions to the life of the department, institution, and the larger community are an essential part of Denison’s mission. We anticipate our new colleague will regularly engage in service activities within these communities. Denison faculty are expected to maintain an active research agenda that results in scholarly publications and supports continued professional growth in order to gain tenure. Denison is a highly selective, residential liberal arts college enrolling approximately 2,400 students from across the nation and around the world. The college is located in the village of Granville, 30 minutes from Columbus, Ohio, the state capital, which hosts a wide range of cultural and artistic opportunities. Granville offers an excellent public school system and easy access to outdoor activities. A supportive environment for teacher-scholars who value both classroom and research excellence, Denison offers extensive support for its faculty, including an annual professional development account, competitive professional development funding, and a one-semester research leave after a successful pre-tenure review. The college also offers opportunities for student-faculty research collaboration, stipends for supervising summer-research students and a range of workshops and mentoring programs to develop our strengths as teacher-scholars.  Denison offers a competitive salary and a comprehensive benefits package, including tuition benefits to attend Denison or other affiliated colleges and a generous retirement contribution. Qualifications: Ph.D. in economics, finance, or related field by start date of appointment, August 2027 (ABD will be considered as Instructor until PhD is attained); potential for strong teaching and active research agenda in the field of macro-finance and/or international finance in a liberal arts college environment. Application Instructions: Dossiers should include a letter of application; CV; statement of teaching philosophy, which addresses the candidate’s approach to teaching economics and finance in a liberal arts setting; writing sample; and three letters of reference. In the application, candidates should highlight their commitment to liberal arts education and address their experience interacting with and mentoring undergraduate students. They should provide evidence of teaching excellence and the ability to create effective active learning experiences in the classroom, including sample teaching evaluations, if available. To be assured of full consideration, please apply by November 23, 2026, when we will begin reviewing applications. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Submit application via Interfolio at: apply.interfolio.com/194126",
      "department": "Economics"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194122": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics/Public Economics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22 Location: Granville, OH The Department of Economics at Denison University invites applications for a tenure-track position in the field of public economics starting August 2027. Strong candidates will demonstrate a commitment to teaching at the undergraduate level and an appreciation of the interdisciplinary nature of a small residential liberal arts institution, as well as a clear and active research agenda in the field of public economics. Primary teaching responsibilities will include an upper-level elective course in public finance; introductory and intermediate courses in microeconomic theory and/or econometrics; and additional policy-related elective courses in the candidate’s area of expertise which complement the existing offerings of the department. The teaching load for this position is 5 courses per academic year. The Department of Economics at Denison has sixteen full-time faculty members who appreciate diverse approaches to economics. The department now offers a B.S. in Finance in addition to the B.A. and minor in Economics. For more information about the department please see: https://denison.edu/academics/economics . Denison University seeks candidates who will contribute to a vibrant academic community characterized by open inquiry, robust debate, and mutual respect. Contributions to the life of the department, institution, and the larger community are an essential part of Denison’s mission. We anticipate our new colleague will regularly engage in service activities within these communities. Denison faculty are expected to maintain an active research agenda that results in scholarly publications and supports continued professional growth in order to gain tenure. Denison is a highly selective, residential liberal arts college enrolling approximately 2,400 students from across the nation and around the world. The college is located in the village of Granville, 30 minutes from Columbus, Ohio, the state capital, which hosts a wide range of cultural and artistic opportunities. Granville offers an excellent public school system and easy access to outdoor activities. A supportive environment for teacher-scholars who value both classroom and research excellence, Denison offers extensive support for its faculty, including an annual professional development account, competitive professional development funding, and a one-semester research leave after a successful pre-tenure review. The college also offers opportunities for student-faculty research collaboration, stipends for supervising summer-research students and a range of workshops and mentoring programs to develop our strengths as teacher-scholars.  Denison offers a competitive salary and a comprehensive benefits package, including tuition benefits to attend Denison or other affiliated colleges and a generous retirement contribution. Qualifications: Ph.D. in economics or related field by start date of appointment, August 2027 (ABD will be considered as Instructor until PhD is attained); potential for strong teaching and active research agenda in the field of public economics in a liberal arts college environment. Application Instructions: Dossiers should include a letter of application; CV; statement of teaching philosophy, which addresses the candidate’s approach to teaching economics in a liberal arts setting; writing sample; and three letters of reference. In the application, candidates should highlight their commitment to liberal arts education and address their experience interacting with and mentoring undergraduate students. They should provide evidence of teaching excellence and the ability to create effective active learning experiences in the classroom, including sample teaching evaluations, if available. To be assured of full consideration, please apply by November 23, 2026, when we will begin reviewing applications. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Submit application via Interfolio at: apply.interfolio.com/194122",
      "department": "Economics"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194432": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Global Commerce",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25 Location: Granville, Ohio The Global Commerce program at Denison University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the assistant or associate professor level beginning in Fall 2027. Global Commerce takes an interdisciplinary approach to the study of business. The program trains students to think broadly and critically about how global exchanges of goods, services, information, and money shape and are shaped by a wide variety of economic, political, cultural, social, and environmental factors. Students in the program put this training into practice through consulting projects, entrepreneurial pitches, and a variety of co-curricular experiences. The current faculty includes scholars in history, economics, anthropology, organizational behavior, English, and philosophy. We are hiring a tenure-track faculty member from the humanities or humanistic social sciences whose research focuses on questions related to business, trade, or economic life. The hire will teach across our core curriculum, which includes an introductory course on the relationship between commerce and society, an introductory course on how businesses function in the modern economy, an intermediate course centering on a local business consulting project, and an advanced global entrepreneurship capstone in which students develop a business plan. Successful candidates will have the opportunity to develop commerce-related electives aligned with their research area. (For more details on the Global Commerce curriculum, please see: https://denison.edu/academics/global-commerce .) The teaching load is 5 courses per year, the largest of which is capped at 25 students. A PhD is required by the time of appointment. A pplicants must demonstrate a commitment to excellence in liberal arts teaching at the undergraduate level, a desire to contribute to the development of the Global Commerce major, and a willingness to work with our colleagues in the Knowlton Center for Career Exploration. Applicants must also demonstrate interest in integrating global perspectives into their teaching and working in an interdisciplinary program. We will consider the extent to which each candidate’s research perspective complements those currently represented in the Department. Applicants must also provide evidence of an active research agenda; continued scholarship is required of all tenure-track and tenured members of the Denison faculty. Additional work experience in the business, government, or non-profit sectors is strongly valued as a complement to academic expertise. Full consideration will be given to applications received by October 30th, 2026 , though we will continue to accept applications until the position is filled. We expect candidates to have their PhD in hand by August 2027. Applicants should submit the following electronic application materials on-line : (1) a cover letter that explains the candidate’s commitment to liberal arts teaching and discusses the candidate’s interest in our interdisciplinary, practically-oriented approach to the study of Global Commerce; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a teaching statement or portfolio that lays out the candidate's teaching philosophy, interests, and experience; (4) a 1-2 page description of the candidate’s research agenda; (5) a writing sample; and (6) a list of three academic references (upon narrowing our pool of candidates, we will ask for letters).",
      "department": "Global Commerce"
    }
  },
